# Digital Dice + IR Remote Mood Lamp!

Combined two things into one sketch: a push-button LCD dice roller and an IR remote-controlled RGB mood lamp with 6 color presets.

## How it works

Dice: press the button, LCD flashes through random numbers (slowing down each loop) then lands on a result 1-6, shown on the LCD.

Lamp: point the remote at the IR receiver, press 1-6, RGB LED switches to that number's preset color.

## Parts

- Arduino Mega 2560
- Push button
- LCD1602 + 10K potentiometer 
- RGB LED + 3 220 omh resistors
- IR receiver + remote

## Pinout

| Component | Pin(s) |
|---|---|
| Button | 2 |
| RGB LED (R/G/B) | 9, 10, 6 |
| IR receiver | 11 |
| LCD (RS, EN, D4-D7) | 22, 23, 4, 5, 8, 7 |
| LCD V0 | potentiometer wiper |

## Libraries

- LiquidCrystal
- IRremote by Armin Joachimsmeyer (Library Manager)

## Notes / things I ran into

- LCD backlight has its own A/K pins separate from VDD/VSS - if the screen stays dark even with power wired right, check those and wire them to the same 5v and ground as the VSS and VVD
- Button legs need to straddle the breadboard's center gap, GND on one side, signal pin on the other - same side shorts them together
